<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gianfrancesco I Gonzaga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1395–1444</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gianfrancesco I Gonzaga (1395–1444) was ruler of Mantua from 1407. In 1433 Emperor Sigismund made him the first Marquis of Mantua, raising the Gonzaga from captains of the people to imperial princes. He served as a condottiere for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>, and invited the humanist Vittorino da Feltre to teach at his court.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gianfrancesco-i-gonzaga.jpg" alt="Gianfrancesco I Gonzaga" width="320" height="437" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gianfrancesco_I_Gonzaga.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
